---
description: Where tests go and which config runs them
globs: tests/**, packages/*/tests/**, **/*.test.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

- Unit: `packages/<pkg>/tests/Unit` only. Integration: `packages/<pkg>/tests/Integration`.
  Feature and Browser: `packages/<pkg>/tests/<Type>` or the root `tests/<Type>` for cross-package scenarios.
  Performance: `packages/<pkg>/tests/Performance/*.perf.test.ts`.
- Every type runs on Vitest (ADR 0010): one project per type in the root `vitest.config.ts`
  (`vitest run --project unit`), import from `'vitest'`. Do not add per-test configs. Browser tests have
  `vitest.browser.config.ts` (Vitest + Playwright, requests to `/__test/echo`, ADR 0009).
- Tests run in plain Node; a file that needs the DOM or XHR starts with `// @vitest-environment jsdom-with-fetch`.
- A folder per subject, a file per scenario: `<Subject>/<Subject>.<method>.<case>.test.ts`.
- Each dot in the file name opens a narrower scope (`Bootstrap.attachment.csv`); a hyphen only joins words of one
  segment (`Http.send.connection-dropped`).
- `describe('<Subject>.<method> should <result>')`, `it('when <condition>')`; negative cases for every subject.
- Arrange-Act-Assert, self-contained files, explicit generic types: section Tests in `AGENTS.md`. Test types: ADR 0005.
- Every change comes with tests: new behaviour gets new files; rewrite an old test only when its API changed.
- A lesson test: `packages/<pkg>/tests/Feature/Examples/Examples.<subject>.<case>.test.ts`, named after the lesson
  folder without its number, one `it.each` over the six variants against `createLessonServer` on port 0.
